==English==
{{was wotd|2008|September|28}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|la|en}} {{m|la|refractārius||obstinate}}, from {{m|la|refractus}}, past participle of {{m|la|refringere||to break up}}. Originally {{m|en|refractary}}, {{m|en|refractarie}}, but reanalysed after other adjectives in {{m|en|-ory}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK|US}} {{IPA|en|/ɹɪˈfɹæk.təɹ.i/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-refractory.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{audio|en|en-au-refractory.ogg|Audio (AU)}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# [[obstinate|Obstinate]] and [[unruly]]; strongly [[opposed]] to something.
#: {{syn|en|contrary|q1=inanimates|fractious|Thesaurus:obstinate}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1787|year_published=1863|author=[[s:Author:Alexander Hamilton|Alexander Hamilton]]|title=[[s:The Federalist Papers|The Federalist]]|chapter=[[s:The Federalist Papers/No. 16|No. 16]]|page=[[s:Page:Federalist, Dawson edition, 1863.djvu/247|103]]|passage={{...}} in most instances attempts to coerce the '''refractory''' and disobedient have been the signals of bloody wars, {{...}}}}
#* '''1836''', [[w:Charles Dickens|Charles Dickens]], ''[[w:The Pickwick Papers|The Pickwick Papers]]'', [[s:The_Pickwick_Papers/Chapter_26|Chapter 26]],
#*: Mr. Weller knocked at the door, and after a pretty long interval—occupied by the party without, in whistling a tune, and by the party within, in persuading a '''refractory''' flat candle to allow itself to be lighted {{...}}
#* '''1913''' Eleanor Porter: ''Pollyanna'': Chapter 8:
#*: For five minutes Pollyanna worked swiftly, deftly, combing a '''refractory''' curl into fluffiness, perking up a drooping ruffle at the neck, or shaking a pillow into plumpness so that the head might have a better pose. Meanwhile the sick woman, frowning prodigiously, and openly scoffing at the whole procedure, was, in spite of herself, beginning to tingle with a feeling perilously near to excitement.
# Not affected by great [[heat]].
#: {{syn|en|heat-resistant}}
#* {{quote-book|en|1855|Frederick Overman|A Treatise on Metallurgy|page=315|url=http://books.google.ca/books?id=92rCLRxAVzkC&pg=PA315&dq=refractory#PPA315,M1|passage=Pure lime is extremely '''refractory''', but readily fusible if any silex is brought in contact with it; {{...}}}}
# {{lb|en|medicine}} [[difficult|Difficult]] to [[treat]].
#* '''1949''', Albert Fields and John Hoesley, "[http://www.pubmedcentral.nih.gov/articlerender.fcgi?tool=pubmed&pubmedid=18131684 Neck and Shoulder Pain]", ''Calif. Med.'', 70(6):478–482.,
#*: Many of the vague and '''refractory''' cases of neck and shoulder pain and of migraine may be due to cervical disc disease.
#* '''1990''', H. A. Ring ''et al'', "[http://www.pubmedcentral.nih.gov/articlerender.fcgi?tool=pubmed&pubmedid=2292696 Vigabatrin: rational treatment for chronic epilepsy]", ''J. Neurol. Neurosurg.Psychiatry'', 53(12):1051–1055,
#*: In 33 adult patients with long standing '''refractory''' epilepsy on treatment with one or two standard anti-convulsant drugs,
# {{lb|en|biology}} [[incapable|Incapable]] of registering a [[reaction]] or [[stimulus]].
#* '''1959''', Nobusada Ishiko and Werner R. Loewenstein, "[http://www.sciencemag.org/cgi/content/abstract/130/3386/1405 Electrical output of a receptor membrane]", ''[[w:Science (journal)|Science]]'', 1959, 130:1405-6,
#*: The production of a generator potential leaves a '''refractory''' state in the receptor membrane {{...}}
#* '''1970''', S.S. Barold ''et al'', "[http://www.pubmedcentral.nih.gov/articlerender.fcgi?artid=487415 Chest wall stimulation in evaluation of patients with implanted ventricular-inhibited demand pacemakers]", ''Br. Heart J.'', 32(6):783–789,
#*: The {{...}} delivery of external stimuli {{...}} delineates the pacemaker '''refractory''' period after the emission of a pacing stimulus and after the sensing of a spontaneous beat.

